From 500ea3516a482b343c1efdd643c9635cef26b97a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jev-router <jev-router@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:32:36 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(providers): read gemini-web answers from the DOM, not the
 dead StreamGenerate URL match
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Gemini's current web build (boq-gemini-web-uiserver_20261015.13_p0, Argon era)
no longer serves the reply on a response URL containing "StreamGenerate": the
generation rides opaque batchexecute/RPC channels whose bodies are no plaintext
wrb.fr frames either. The executor's page.on("response") listener therefore
never matches, waits out its 30s race, and returns 502 "No response from Gemini"
on every request (upstream #10751, #16575 — both closed waiting for exactly this
capture; a signed-in headless session answers normally while no StreamGenerate
request fires at all).

Replace the network sniffing with a DOM reader: poll the last
model-response-text block until it loses processing-state-visible, the
thinking-dots/pending-response placeholders are gone, the Stop button is gone,
and the text is stable across two polls, with the caller's abort signal
honored each poll and a 120s cap. Transport-agnostic: survives rpcid renames
and response encryption.

Follow-up fixes found by live testing against a signed-in account (2026-10-16):
- page.evaluate takes exactly ONE argument (the multi-arg call threw
  "Too many arguments" -> every request 500'd)
- Enter no longer submits the composer under automation; the send button
  (aria-label "Send message") does — click it, fall back to Enter

Extracted as pure, unit-testable functions (collectGeminiDomState,
clickGeminiSendButtonInPage); existing fakes updated to the new contract,
regression tests added for the polling rules and the single-arg/click paths.
